 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Part two. The attic hatch is *open*, a black square in the ceiling.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Sam climbs a chair with the flashlight. Dust, beams, cold air.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Nobody. Just a smell of wet wool.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "He nails the hatch shut and they don't sleep.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "In the morning there's a *newspaper* on the kitchen table.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "It's from a town forty miles away, dated three weeks ago.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "They never bought it. The road has been closed for days.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then the food starts to disappear. Bread. A whole ham. Candles.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Stay, because Sam set a trap that night.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "He hangs a little *bell* on the nails of the hatch.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "If anything moves it, they'll know.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "At 3:12 AM, the bell rings once.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then a voice comes through the ceiling, quiet and calm.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "It repeats their dinner conversation, *word for word*.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Jess's laugh. Sam's joke about the hunter. In their exact voices.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Jess grabs the car keys. Sam grabs the axe.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "And the voice upstairs says, in Jess's voice: grab the keys.",
   "pausa": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then the hatch nails start to bend. Part three, {when_next}.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
